1. First, understand the whole picture

Imagine your computer is a company.

| Computer part    | Company example       | What it does                            |
| ---------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| **User**         | Employee              | Gives instructions                      |
| **Applications** | Different departments | Do useful work                          |
| **Shell**        | Receptionist          | Accepts commands                        |
| **Linux Kernel** | Manager               | Controls resources and coordinates work |
| **Hardware**     | Company resources     | CPU, RAM, disk, network card            |

The kernel is the manager. Applications ask it to do things, and the kernel communicates with the hardware.

